 for beach resorts along the Costa Brava, Girona is the closest airport.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Girona","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Girona","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Girona is a walled medieval city in Spain, listed as a conjunto historico and easy to reach. Catedral de Girona heads the list, with Sant Pere de Galligants and Casa Maso behind it. Ten hours covers the old town; May to August is the stretch.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":100266,"visit_h":9.6}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-catedral-de-girona","name":"Catedral de Girona","kind":"Cathedral","lat":41.98751,"lon":2.82608,"dist_km":0.5,"sig":2.975,"rank_score":11.3,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Templo católico de Cataluña (España)","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Girona_Cathedral_2020.jpg/960px-Girona_Cathedral_2020.jpg","author":"Fernando","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Girona_Cathedral_2020.jpg","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catedral_de_Santa_Mar%C3%ADa_(Gerona)","heritage":true,"merged_from":["Girona Cathedral"]},{"id":"hl-sant-julia-de-ramis","name":"Sant Julià de Ramis","kind":"Landmark","lat":42.02802,"lon":2.854,"dist_km":5.5,"sig":2.483,"rank_score":10.41,"resolved_by":"retyped","fact":"Municipality in Catalonia, Spain","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/SantJuliaRamis2.jpg/960px-SantJuliaRamis2.jpg","author":"Araceli Merino","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SantJuliaRamis2.jpg","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sant_Juli%C3%A0_de_Ramis","heritage":true},{"id":"hl-sant-pere-de-galligants","name":"Sant Pere de Galligants","kind":"Monastery","lat":41.98874,"lon":2.82661,"dist_km":0.6,"sig":2.483,"rank_score"